# modos-cpu environment variables.
#
# Copy this file to `.env` in the same directory as the binary (or the repo
# root when running `go run`). The server loads it automatically at startup
# WITHOUT overriding variables that are already set in the real environment.
#
# Lines starting with `#` are comments. Use `KEY=value` per line. Values can
# be wrapped in single or double quotes if they contain spaces.

# ─── Admin panel ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Leave all three blank to disable the /admin panel entirely. When any of
# them is missing the panel returns the same 404 page as any other unknown
# route, so the surface is not advertised.

# Plain-text username for the admin login form.
ADMIN_USER=

# bcrypt hash of the admin password. Generate it with:
#   go run ./cmd/modos-cpu admin-hash -pass='your-secret-here'
ADMIN_PASS_HASH=

# 32+ random characters. Signs admin cookies, salts the stored IP hashes and
# derives the key that encrypts secrets saved from the admin panel. Generate
# it with `make session-secret` or `openssl rand -hex 32`. The server logs a
# warning at startup when it is missing or shorter than 32 characters.
SESSION_SECRET=

# ─── Persistence ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Optional override for the SQLite database path. When unset the server
# falls back to $XDG_STATE_HOME/modos-cpu/state.db (or ~/.local/state/...).
# MODOS_STATE_DB=/var/lib/modos-cpu/state.db

# ─── Capacity ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Maximum concurrent public sessions before /full is shown.
# MAX_PUBLIC_SESSIONS=10

# Maximum concurrent privileged (invite-based) sessions.
# MAX_PRIVILEGED_SESSIONS=5

# ─── Simulator ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# How many CPU cores each Simulator spawns. 1 reproduces the classic
# single-core kernel; 2–4 enables the multicore demos (race_counter,
# safe_counter, …) and the upcoming /concurrencia view. Clamped to [1, 4].
# MODOS_CPU_CORES=1

# ─── Timeouts ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Idle session timeout (Go duration string: 30m, 1h, ...).
# SESSION_TTL=30m

# How long an admin-issued invite link stays usable.
# INVITE_TTL=24h

# How often the cleanup goroutine prunes idle sessions and expired tokens.
# CLEANUP_INTERVAL=1m

# ─── Origins ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Comma-separated host patterns accepted on WebSocket upgrades. The match is
# against the host portion of the Origin header (no scheme). Wildcards are
# allowed via `*`. Defaults to localhost:5173 (Vite dev) and localhost:9080
# (embedded build). Production deployments behind a real domain must set this.
# ALLOWED_ORIGINS=cpu.example.com,*.example.com

# ─── Reverse proxy ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Name of the header that carries the real client IP, set by the proxy in
# front of the server. Leave empty when clients connect directly: forwarded
# headers are then ignored, so nobody can spoof their IP to dodge the rate
# limits. Use CF-Connecting-IP behind Cloudflare, X-Real-IP behind the
# bundled nginx example. Only set it when every request goes through that
# proxy.
# TRUSTED_PROXY_HEADER=CF-Connecting-IP

# ─── Login protection ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Student logins allowed per IP every 15 minutes (default 5). Raise it for
# classrooms where many students share one public IP.
# AUTH_LOGIN_LIMIT=5

# Cloudflare Turnstile keys for the student login form. Both can also be set
# from the admin panel. Leave empty to disable the challenge.
# TURNSTILE_SITEKEY=
# TURNSTILE_SECRET=

# Store the plain client IP next to its hash in session history (admin view).
# ADMIN_REVEAL_IP=false

# ─── ARCHIUS tutor ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The tutor needs a chat model and an embeddings provider. Every value here
# can be overridden from the admin panel.
#
# Chat provider: gemini (default), deepseek, groq or openai_compat.
# LLM_PROVIDER=gemini
# LLM_MODEL=
# LLM_BASE_URL=
# GEMINI_API_KEY=
# DEEPSEEK_API_KEY=
# GROQ_API_KEY=
# LLM_API_KEY=
# Global requests per minute towards the chat provider (0 = unlimited).
# LLM_RPM=0
#
# Embeddings provider: ollama or jina.
# EMBEDDER_PROVIDER=ollama
# OLLAMA_HOST=http://localhost:11434
# OLLAMA_EMBED_MODEL=bge-m3
# JINA_API_KEY=
# Concurrent embedding requests (keeps free-tier providers under their limit).
# EMBEDDER_MAX_CONCURRENCY=2
#
# Prior conversation turns sent with each question (0-10, default 3).
# TUTOR_HISTORY_WINDOW_TURNS=3
